WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:06.610
The new stars at the Berlin zoo are relaxing
and settling into their home.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:11.009
Newcomers Jiao Qing and Meng Meng have made
it past the strains of their journey over

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:17.090
from China.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.640
The arrival of the two panda bears at Berlin's
airport was highly anticipated.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.810
Especially by the director of the Berlin Zoo.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.170
"This is because of the rarity of the animals.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.109
They are a highly endangered species, that
has a hard time getting by in nature."

00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:36.829
Fewer than 2000 of them live in the wild.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:39.559
And they can only be found in China.

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:43.920
Female pandas are able to conceive for just
a couple of days a year, meaning reproduction

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.050
is rare.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:51.510
Conservation workers have instituted breeding
programs to encourage more births.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.109
Panda bears spend most of their time eating.

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:58.140
The pair in Berlin is given 80 kilograms of
bamboo per day.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:04.190
But that's far from their most remarkable
quality, says China's ambassador to Germany.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.550
"Panda bears are holy in China.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.500
Panda bears are also the ambassadors of friendship
and loyalty."

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.890
Beijing is fully aware of the effect these
cute animals have, and so have been sending

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.500
their panda bears on tour around the world
for decades.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.409
One example was in the 70s when U.S. President
Nixon visited arch enemy China.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:32.140
A short time later the Washington zoo received
the gift of their first panda bears - as a

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:37.119
thank you and gesture of reconciliation.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.840
The People's Republic continued to use the
system of cuddly diplomacy to reward governments

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.630
for economic or political cooperation.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:51.130
Or to solidify ties of friendship between
China and other countries.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.549
In 1999, two years after Hong Kong had been
returned to China, Chinese former vice-premier

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:04.159
Wu Yi gave Hong Kong's government head Tung
Chee Hwa the giant pandas An An and Jia Jia.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:09.289
Two years ago, China promised to give the
Berlin Zoo the pandas while Chancellor Angela

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:10.790
Merkel was visiting.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.459
She had been accompanied by investors.

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:19.319
Panda bears Meng meng and Jiao Qing are set
to stay in the Berlin Zoo for 15 years.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:24.319
But with a caveat: China has the right to
take the bears back home anytime, if the Beijing

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:27.370
government sees reason to do so.

